{title: Lord, Dismiss Us with Thy Blessing}
{artist: Robert Hawker / Charles C. Converse}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 103}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Praise Book, edited by Howard B. Grose & George B. Graff ( Boston, Massachusetts: United Society of Christian Endeavor, 1906), # 2)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Lord, dismiss us with Thy [D]blessing;
[A]Bid us now depart in [E]peace;
[A]Still on heav’nly manna [D]feeding,
[A]Let [E]our faith and love in[A]crease.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Fill each heart with conso[D]lation;
[A]Up to Thee our hearts we [E]raise;
[A]When we reach our blissful [D]station,
[A]Then [E]we’ll give Thee nobler [A]praise.
{end_of_verse}
